EGL offscreen platform for OpenGLide (wsh-pve, LGPL-2.1 like OpenGLide)

With setConfig(WRAPPER_FLAG_OFFSCREEN) (0x100), grSstWinOpen() opens no X display: it creates a
desktop OpenGL compatibility context on an EGL display without a window (Mesa's surfaceless
platform, else the first EGL device, else the default display) and renders into a framebuffer
object whose colour attachments 0 and 1 are Glide's back and front buffers (OGLBuffer() maps
GL_BACK/GL_FRONT at the four places that select a buffer). grBufferSwap() copies back to front.
The host program reads the front buffer with the new exports getOffscreenSize() and
getOffscreenFrame() (BGRX, rows bottom up). Without the flag nothing changes (X11/GLX).
Gamma ramps and MSAA are not applied offscreen yet. Applied by build.sh to qemu-xtra's openglide/.
